ith a nearby word. A direct relation can still be a false assertion: keep conflict and semantic fit separate.\nInput: {\"question\": \"What is the profession of Ingrid Visser?\", \"slot_hint\": \"other\", \"all_original_sources\": {\"D1S1\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0034-9719cd5b982f:d00\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 26, \"text\": \"focusing on orca research.\"}, \"D1S2\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0034-9719cd5b982f:d00\", \"start\": 27, \"end\": 105, \"text\": \"She also set up Adopt an Orca to facilitate fund raising and public awareness.\"}, \"D1S3\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0034-9719cd5b982f:d00\", \"start\": 106, \"end\": 321, \"text\": \"Visser has written an autobiography, \\\"Swimming with Orca\\\", which was a finalist in the Environmental category of the New Zealand Montana Book Awards, and two children’s books (\\\"I Love Killer Whales\\\" and \\\"The Orca\\\").\"}, \"D1S4\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0034-9719cd5b982f:d00\", \"start\": 322, \"end\": 433, \"text\": \"The latter has been translated into Māori and is currently in press as a bilingual English/Spanish publication.\"}, \"D1S5\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0034-9719cd5b982f:d00\", \"start\": 434, \"end\": 547, \"text\": \"Visser works as a guide on a variety of eco-tourism adventures, from swimming with whales to visiting Antarctica.\"}, \"D1S6\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0034-9719cd5b982f:d00\", \"start\": 548, \"end\": 577, \"text\": \"She is also a public speaker.\"}, \"D1S7\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0034-9719cd5b982f:d00\", \"start\": 578, \"end\": 613, \"text\": \"Visser is a member of the Australia\"}}, \"original_cards\": [], \"R5_answers\": [\"orca researcher\", \"eco-tourism guide\", \"public speaker\", \"author\"], \"candidates\": [{\"id\": \"C0\", \"answer\": \"orca researcher\", \"origin\": \"R5\"}, {\"id\": \"C1\", \"answer\": \"eco-to